  <ym-title|Trace proof correspondence (draft)><label|trace-proof-correspondence-draft>

  Source revision: 3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464. Parent author
  session: hairer-codex-existence-20261111.

  <verbatim|manuscript/existence/trace-profiles.tex> follows full reads of
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Wick/{Expansion,Gain,Massive,PolynomialField,Log,Refute}.lean>.
  Its principal declarations are <verbatim|YM.TraceExtension.Wick.Expands.mult>,
  <verbatim|primitives>, <verbatim|moment_d>, <verbatim|euler>,
  <verbatim|differentiated>, <verbatim|basic_expands>,
  <verbatim|moment_expands>, <verbatim|Mode.field_value>,
  <verbatim|Track.moments_expand>, <verbatim|no_powerlog>,
  <verbatim|real_profile>, and <verbatim|euclidean_excludes>.

  The main steps are preserved: finite power-log algebra, derivative
  comparison for primitive remainders, radial Euler identity and order
  bootstrap (including the exceptional -1 order), polar angular factor, and
  dyadic lexicographic leading-term obstruction. Standard elementary
  integration by parts replaces the Gamma-integral library call. No
  convergent asymptotic series is assumed. This proves the public
  finite-profile exclusion conditional on a positive trace asymptotic. It
  does not yet prove that asymptotic, nor the stronger internal
  momentum-test/Wick-palette/Maxwell exclusions.

  Independent gpt-6-astra review passed fingerprint
  6a708c5fae0e1f07849c527dd4645f402ce753db088533972eba39ffe32c9d54. Machine
  review fields remain null; this is not human acceptance.

  <section|Numerical coefficient, physical normalization, and all-radius
  passage><label|numerical-coefficient-physical-normalization-and-all-radius-passage>

  <verbatim|trace-asymptotic.tex> follows full reads of
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/Foundation/Constant.lean>,
  <verbatim|Foundation/Dilate.lean>, <verbatim|Chart/{Masts,North,Nectar,Time,Line}.lean>,
  and <verbatim|Verse/{Pears,Round,Day,Cape}.lean>. The central declarations
  are <verbatim|YM.Trace.curl_squares>, <verbatim|wick_norm>;
  <verbatim|YM.Trace.Over.ranking>, <verbatim|year_spec>, <verbatim|july>,
  <verbatim|Store_l>; and <verbatim|YM.Trace.Verse.rounds>,
  <verbatim|greens>, <verbatim|rainbow>, <verbatim|axis_shape>,
  <verbatim|tagline>, <verbatim|monotone_axis>, <verbatim|border>,
  <verbatim|outside>.

  The chapter proves the ordered-axis Wick coefficient, rank-nullity
  reduction, nonzero flux test fixing scalar amplitude, vanishing unit
  correction, finite-basis moving-label limit, normalization factor, exact
  radial reduction, positive-spectral monotonicity squeeze at generic
  diagonal shots, and the bad-sequence contradiction removing scale
  subsequences. It preserves these source main steps. It does NOT claim to
  prove ChoiceK/reveals, the detecting observer and Ward jet estimates,
  Gondola/seat quantitative receipts, Gallery scale selection. Those inputs
  are explicitly displayed in ordinary mathematical form. The specialized
  TraceSpectrum measure is now constructed in the subsequent section of this
  evidence record. The source's <verbatim|force_b> uses the definition
  <verbatim|d2 = forceR> and <verbatim|beta_eq>; its physical interpretation
  relies on the unresolved stress calibration. The exact curvature covariance
  convention is <verbatim|YM.Maxwell.normal> from
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Maxwell/PotentialKernel.lean>, equal to 1/(4 pi^2).

  Initial trace-asymptotic review passed ea67b21fa62625532697710fd0ca52bc36facb76deedfae2a2508c9d60bd82d6.
  The subsequent removal of its specialized spectral-measure input in favor
  of the new proof below passed renewed review at 5153c8ba (full hash in
  review report). No new external literature search was needed for these
  elementary proofs.

  <section|Point-field spectral measure><label|point-field-spectral-measure>

  <verbatim|trace-spectrum.tex> follows full reads of
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Heat/{Lift,Duration}.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Paley/{Icon,Mapped}.lean> and
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/TraceExtension/{Damping,PolynomialGrowth,Relative,Momentum,Centered,WilsonTrace}.lean>.
  Principal declarations: <verbatim|YM.Paley.empty>, <verbatim|along_edge>,
  <verbatim|heat>; <verbatim|YM.OS.Semigroup.heat>, <verbatim|damp>;
  <verbatim|YM.TraceExtension.self_ample>, <verbatim|pointState_add>,
  <verbatim|pair_restricted>, <verbatim|undamp>, <verbatim|damp>,
  <verbatim|pair_at>, <verbatim|energy_bounded>, <verbatim|falling>,
  <verbatim|spectral_temperate>, <verbatim|surface_integral>,
  <verbatim|norm_read>, <verbatim|mass_read>, <verbatim|weights_injective>,
  <verbatim|spectral_forward>, <verbatim|spectral_placed>,
  <verbatim|trace_turn>, <verbatim|trace_adj>, <verbatim|scalar_rail>,
  <verbatim|vev_boundary>, and <verbatim|traceSpectrum_exists>.

  All major steps are proved, using the earlier heat/Gram/slab/boundary and
  field representation chapters. No specialized trace positive measure is
  assumed. The source's Gaussian boundary-uniqueness proof is preserved. The
  forward cone is transferred from actual field PVM measures by Fourier
  weights equal to one on compact balls, not asserted for the auxiliary
  chamber. Trace scalar/self-adjoint/centered properties remain conditional
  on the actual real symmetric tensorial stress and Ward structure, whose
  construction is still outstanding. Independent review passed
  2f2c16737f123073f07ec3e5132fd4c6df83ad8021d20fa44d2d32aaece494e7.

